            <!-- MAPS-->
            <!--PYRAMID OF FAILURE-->
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_PYRAMID_OF_FAILURE_ID</LocID>                                     <Text>PYRAMID OF FAILURE</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_PYRAMID_OF_FAILURE_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                            <Text>The climb was easy — but what rises fast, falls just as swiftly.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_PYRAMID_OF_FAILURE_INTRO</LocID>                                  <Text>You started from nothing — step by step, you climbed to the top and became the boss. But as time passed, everyone turned against you, working behind your back. Now they’ve made their move, and it’s up to you to take back control of the entire region. Almost everything is gone, but as the boss, you're still the only one with exclusive access to the keys of the colored gates. However, there are also the so-called grey gates — which only open when...</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_PYRAMID_OF_FAILURE_VICTORY</LocID>                                <Text>From the bottom to the top — and from the top, back down to the depths. You made it through, and now you're back in control. Once again, you're the boss of all bosses!</Text>    </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>MESSAGE_PYRAMID_OF_FAILURE_GATE</LocID>                              <Text>Look, the gate is opening!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>

            
            <!--OH RATS-->
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_OH_RATS_ID</LocID>                                                <Text>Oh Rats</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_RATS_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                                          <Text>What happens when you don't take care of your pest problem? It only grows and when you don't act, it can be too late.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_RATS_INTRO</LocID>                                                <Text>Rats infestation is the worst in these parts, and we need you to clean it. And what is the best way to fight fire? Yes, with fire. Take your commander, recruit anyone and clean these lands.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_RATS_VICTORY</LocID>                                              <Text>Victory! You managed to clean the infestation. Now it's time for your reward, you can pick it up at our slaughterhouse.</Text>    </GameDBLocalizedString>
  
  
            <!--DUEL-->
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_DUEL_ID</LocID>                                                   <Text>Duel</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_DUEL_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                                          <Text>One-on-one, two irreconcilable opponents face off.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_DUEL_INTRO</LocID>                                                <Text>Two separate territories connected by an ancient bridge — a path that opens only during the first phase of each cycle. A duel that will forever determine who is superior.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_DUEL_VICTORY</LocID>                                              <Text>Your opponent has fallen — how does it feel to be the victor? Is it just 1:0, or are you playing best out of five?</Text>    </GameDBLocalizedString>

            <!--CREMATORIA-->
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_CREMATORIA_ID</LocID>                                             <Text>Crematoria</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_CREMATORIA_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                                    <Text>Not very hospitable part of this planet, where standing still will cost you your life. Perfect spot for adrenaline junkies or as punishment.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_CREMATORIA_INTRO</LocID>                                          <Text>You have been sent here for your crimes. Talking back to your superiors is something you just don't do. Nobody knows what exactly is in the Nebbia di guerra here, but if you are caught in it, you won't come out. So you better move. There are supposed to be some safe havens along the way, where you can rest for a bit, but your best chance is to escape to orbit.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_CREMATORIA_VICTORY</LocID>                                        <Text>Victory! You survived and escaped. This time!</Text>    </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_CREMATORIA_SAVE_MESSAGE</LocID>                                   <Text>Looks like I will be safe here. At least for a while.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_CREMATORIA_STARTING_AGAIN_MESSAGE_1</LocID>                       <Text>Oh no, its starting again.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_CREMATORIA_HURRY_UP_MESSAGE_1</LocID>                             <Text>I should hurry, don't want get trapped here!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_CREMATORIA_STARTING_AGAIN_MESSAGE_2</LocID>                       <Text>It was nice, while it lasted.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_CREMATORIA_HURRY_UP_MESSAGE_2</LocID>                             <Text>Let's move!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>OBJECTIVE_CREMATORIA_FOW_WARNING_SKIRMISH</LocID>                    <Text>Stay out the dangerous areas, they will be covered by deadly FOW!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>OBJECTIVE_CREMATORIA_ESCAPE_SKIRMISH</LocID>                         <Text>Find orbital teleport and escape!</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>CANT_TAKE_OVER_FRIENDLY_BUILDINGS</LocID>                            <Text>This is a friendly building you can't take over.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>

            <!--DUNES-->
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_DUNES</LocID>                                                     <Text>Dunes</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_DUNES_DESCRIPTION</LocID>                                         <Text>Dunes, dust and howling wind. That's what you will face when you explore the abandoned facilities and mines to collect the vast quantity of resources. The environment of this planet should grant you enough time to create an invincible army and defeat all opponents.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_DUNES_INTRO</LocID>                                               <Text>Up to six rivals can meet down here. Your task is clear, enter the dunes, seize valuable facilities, gain advantage over your opponents and defeat all hostile forces in the area.</Text>  </GameDBLocalizedString>
            <GameDBLocalizedString>         <LocID>EA_DUNES_VICTORY</LocID>                                             <Text>Excellent! All enemy forces has been sent to the afterlife! Enjoy this moment while it lasts!</Text>    </GameDBLocalizedString>


